lines=["# #028C — Uniqueness generator","","**Done locally.** Based on accepted `4880c3b`, branch `feature/local-environment-setup`. AI copy is **not connected**. Credits used: **0**. Actual provider calls: **0**. No new npm dependencies, routes, migration, deployment or push.","","## What changed","","Explicit regeneration through the existing #023 action now reserves a stable seed, one of four Looks, six a/b/c section layouts and authored copy. Existing sites retain their exact output until explicitly regenerated. Merely opening a site, saving it, adopting its manifest or publishing it does not activate this feature.","","The seed reuses the existing stored site seed or derives one with `stableSiteStyleSeed(siteId)`. No time, UUID or random value selects rendered content. The selector walks all 2,916 combinations in deterministic order, honors saved contractor Look first and staff overrides next, rejects repeated section structures, then seeks at least three differing picks from every same-trade draft/published snapshot. It records each rule-driven fallback and the best available distance if the constrained pool is exhausted. A saved reservation survives changes to neighboring sites. Concurrent requests reserve against an optimistic per-trade lock in the existing JSON record store, atomically with the tenant update.","","The manifest records seed/source, style, six section IDs, six copy IDs and exact text, copy version, factual identity, overrides and authenticated staff actor, Look provenance, fallback reasons/counts, structural purposes/patterns and uniqueness results. Comparisons include total sites/snapshots, pool fingerprint and the 32 nearest snapshots. A later explicit Look save retains its layouts, records the actor and reassesses its actual distance; an exhausted result is reconsidered at the next regeneration. Existing historical Looks have no invented author.","","`replayUniqueChoices(originalFacts, manifest)` restores the same rendered result, including the existing secondary composition choices. Normal factual edits refresh the authored copy without silently rerolling layouts. The AI path remains off; the generation panel says **AI copy not connected**. Client-forged generated records or picks are rejected.","","### Staff overrides","","Use the existing authenticated `POST /api/tenants/:id/generation` action with `action: \"regenerate\"`, the current row `version`, and optional `overrides: {seed: 123, style: \"bold\", sections: {hero: \"b\", process: \"c\"}}`. Only staff administrators may submit overrides; the server records their identity. Seeds are integers 0–4294967295. A contractor’s saved Look wins over any conflicting staff style. Conflicting fixed page rules return a clear validation error; disabling the final Contact section must be resolved before regeneration. No new selector or settings route was added.","","### Authored copy catalog","","Three versioned choices per slot × six slots × 17 trades = **306 catalog entries**. IDs follow `<kit>.<slot>.v1.a|b|c`. All fact interpolation is escaped. Missing facts select usable neutral wording; no fabricated reviews, years, licenses, counts, offers, prices, awards, urgency or deadlines. Copy purposes differ by section. The catalog uses proper display names such as HVAC and Roofing. The existing variant-a renderer functions are unchanged; an opt-in composition layer applies saved generated copy after the accepted renderer.","","| Slot | Three authored choices | Facts / missing-data behavior | Purpose |","|---|---|---|---|"]
for row in copyrows:lines.append("| "+" | ".join(row)+" |")
lines += ["","### Reused and preserved","","Reused #028A Looks/tokens/fonts, #028B a/b/c compositors, process artwork, photographs/posters/film catalog, #023 manifest/locks/history, existing routes and draft/publish boundary, financing calculator/legal text, forms, and review filtering/full-source aggregates. Generated reviews use the existing no-source and zero-after-filter omission rules. Sample previews retain their labeling. Pending films still publish their installed posters.","","Only regenerated pages load the new scoped `generated-site.css`. It fixes actual generated-combination contrast issues in review surfaces, Current buttons/service cards, chapter rail, financing benefit/step text and form borders; it supplies a visible focus ring. The original 52 CSS source files have no Git changes. All 279 accepted rendered hashes plus platform.css and 374 archived responses remain byte-identical. No existing CSS or variant-a function body was restyled. Raw HTML/CSS captures use ticket-local Git attributes to preserve their exact served bytes without line-ending conversion.","","## Fictional Sample proof","","These are local test fixtures, never real businesses or published sites. All names explicitly say Sample Fictional; review responses are local mocks. They have different Southern California cities and service mixes, no invented business history/license/offer, and Paper Lantern has no review source. Seeds derive directly from their saved fixture IDs, with no staff override.","","| Fictional contractor | City / services | Seed / Look | Hero / services / process / financing / reviews / CTA | Captures |","|---|---|---|---|---|"]
